Package: monitoraSom
Type: Package
Title: Toolbox for Automated Sound Detection Applied to Bioacoustics and
    Passive Acoustic Monitoring
Version: 1.2.0.1
Authors@R: c(person("Gabriel L. M.", "Rosa", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "gabrielrosa@conservasom.com.br", comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-5332-9713")), person("Juan P.", "Zurano", role = "aut", email = "", comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-4201-4366")), person("Ingrid M. D.", "Torres", role = "aut", email = "ingriddenobile@conservasom.com.br", comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-4336-0682")), person("Cassio R.", "Simoes", role = "aut", email = "cassiorachid@conservasom.com.br", comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-1563-575X")), person("Carlos B.", "de Araujo", role = "aut", email = "cabarau@gmail.com", comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-0862-119X")), person("Luiz dos", "Anjos", role = c("aut", "fnd"), email = "lanjos@uel.br", comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-8680-2375")))
Description: Provides a complete workflow to overcome the challenges of
    automated sound recognition and validation in bioacoustics. It includes
    tools for segmentation, validation, and performance evaluation. Among its
    core functionalities are graphical interfaces designed to accelerate manual
    segmentation of soundscape recordings and detection validation. In addition,
    the package includes dedicated tools for validation diagnostics, offering
    quantitative assessments of detection performance. By addressing gaps in
    currently available tools, it promotes data reproducibility and ensures
    methodological rigor. The modular design of the functions supports
    customization, encourages methodological experimentation, and reduces the
    learning curve associated with scripting, empowering users to focus on
    ecological insights rather than technical hurdles.
